   "id": "beitzah.15a.5",
   "daf": "15a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְלֹא מִנְעָל שֶׁאֵינוֹ תָּפוּר. פְּשִׁיטָא! לֹא נִצְרְכָא, דְּאַף עַל גַּב דְּנָקֵיט בְּסִיכֵּי.",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches: «Nor» may one send «an unsewn shoe» on a Festival. The Gemara asks: This is «obvious,» as these shoes are unfit for wearing. The Gemara answers: This statement «was necessary» only to teach «that although» the shoe «is attached with pins» and can be worn, it may not be sent on a Festival. Since it is not properly sewn, it is not usually worn."
  }
